+
+## Resident Session withdrawal (DOM-02)
+
+The existing installation/configuration and grant writers remain the only owners. A resident Host
+keeps its startup package identities and names, but reads current availability before publishing
+plugin tool/Skill descriptions and before dispatch. Disable/uninstall withdraw MCP and Skills;
+revoking an executable-surface grant withdraws MCP/hooks while preserving Skills and commands,
+as the existing grant contract requires. Re-enable/re-approval restores only that Session's
+original contributions. New packages or changed declarations require normal fresh discovery.
+
+```text
+existing settings writer → configuration/install/grant files → existing availability projection
+                                                    → current descriptions / final dispatch gate
+```
+
+MCP connection/recovery and permission waits do not freeze permission to execute. A Host-only
+callback rechecks availability immediately before transport dispatch, including recovery retries.
+No callback crosses MCP/UI wire formats. Already dispatched effects and their durable results
+remain unchanged; withdrawal neither undoes nor replays them. Tool names, rule names, shared
+connections, credentials, Session history and plugin data retain their existing owners.
+
+Skill discovery, catalog and prompt metadata filter the retained startup catalog. Load checks
+again before returning instructions, so an old description or queued Skill call is no grant.
+Previously loaded instructions remain historical evidence; this mechanism cannot erase text
+already delivered to a model, and it does not widen permissions for operations named by Skills.
+
+Acceptance uses public Session execution with a synthetic model and a real local stdio MCP,
+under temporary profile/storage paths. Disable, executable grant revoke, uninstall, re-enable,
+re-approval, waiting calls, cold reopen and persisted tool/Skill results are covered. No paid
+provider or real profile/credential is used.
+
+The original ZCode startup path (`core/runtime/methods/mcp.ts`, `context.ts`) registers MCP
+and stores Skill metadata once. The correction reuses those retained identities, existing
+configuration signature/discovery and per-request context prefix projection. Latest retained
+HarnessRouter `protocol/versions/2026-09-28/plugins.md:343` withholds disabled materialization;
+Kimi's `packages/agent-core-v2/src/agent/plugin/agentPluginService.ts:43,168` instead keeps a Session
+snapshot until `/new` or `/reload`. Fleet's DOM-02 requires resident withdrawal, so those snapshot
+semantics are evidence rather than the selected behavior. MCP SDK stdio `send` waits for request
+metadata and HTTP official-auth waits for headers; a private adapter AsyncLocalStorage carries
+only the current call's callback across those awaits. It checks outbound tool/resource requests,
+never responses, cancellation notifications or other required protocol messages. No available
+MCP request context previously carried a callback outside the wire metadata.
